{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"dbd75cb2f074486d","type":"text","text":"**What is the Dashboard in your project?**\n\nIt is your \"Visual Command Center.\" Instead of staring at dry lines of code in VS Code, you open the Dashboard (via Streamlit) and see:\n\n- **Interactive sliders:** You change the values of site boundaries A and B, and the geometry on the screen rebuilds instantly.\n    \n- **Viewport:** This is where your site's rectangle and the colored building blocks (Power Block, Cooling Tower, etc.) are drawn.\n    \n- **Scoring panel:** Next to the image, you see an evaluation. For example: \"Score: 85/100. Error: Cooling Tower is too close to the Admin Building.\"\n    \n- **Action buttons:** For example, a button to \"Generate 5 new variations\" or \"Export to CAD.\"\n    \n\n**Why are we doing this gradually?**\n\nIf we try to write the code for 60 buildings all at once while factoring in all the rules from your Excel spreadsheet—your brain will fry. Our \"baby steps\" plan looks like this:\n\n- **Step 1:** Just learn how to draw an empty site rectangle in the Dashboard.\n    \n- **Step 2:** Learn how to draw the 3 main \"footprints\" inside it (our groups: Power Block, Cooling Tower, and Admin Building).\n    \n- **Step 3:** Teach the program to \"feel\" the distance between them (that exact 50 meters from your spreadsheet).","x":1600,"y":760,"width":1055,"height":537},
		{"id":"e05dc9ad5733ca89","type":"text","text":"","x":1600,"y":380,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"14369d86ae2ca3cb","type":"text","text":"I downloaded:\n\n## 1) Python \nhttps://realpython.com/python-virtual-environments-a-primer/#create-it\n\n## 2) Streamlit\nhttps://docs.streamlit.io/get-started/installation/command-line\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rMLwiVrK3Fw&list=PLMi6KgK4_mk2rK5jD-BK5RigFIP2QSq8W\n\n**Что такое Environment (виртуальное окружение)?** Представь, что это отдельный «контейнер» или «комната» специально для твоего проекта **PowerPlan AI**. Все библиотеки (Streamlit, Matplotlib), которые мы установим, останутся только в этой комнате и не сломают ничего на твоем компьютере.\n\nWhere to keep?\nLayout_Gen_Design/              \n│\n├── 📦 .venv/                   ← Твое виртуальное окружение (создается само)\n├── 📝 Notes/                   \n├── 🐍 Core/                    \n├── 📥 Data/                    \n└── 📊 Dashboard/\n\nSet\npython -m venv .venv\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\activate\n\n(Если всё получилось, в терминале слева появится зеленая надпись `(.venv)`. Это значит, ты внутри!)\n\nDownload \npip install streamlit matplotlib pandas openpyxl\n\n## 3) Matplotlib\nустановили вместе с streamlit\n","x":520,"y":1141,"width":790,"height":959},
		{"id":"ceae6e826d95e20e","type":"file","file":"02_Library/Prompts_Master/Prompt_History_Phase_01.md","x":1600,"y":1421,"width":1055,"height":400},
		{"id":"0f0031e9f4761233","type":"file","file":"01_Products/Layout_Gen_Design/Pipeline/Phase_01/Phase 01 Output Example.png","x":2880,"y":1475,"width":639,"height":293},
		{"id":"ec6428e9d629d393","type":"text","text":"📋 **Rule Analysis for Your Project**\n\n**1. The Road Network is the skeleton:**\n\n- **Primary Road:** A ring road around the entire site. The setback from the boundary is 5m, and the width is 8m.\n    \n- **Inner Road:** A mandatory road around the Power Block.\n    \n- **Distances:** Roads must be a minimum of 3m away from buildings and 2m away from the Pipe Racks.\n    \n\n**2. Main Groups (Your 3 pillars for Step 01):**\n\n- **Power Block (Units 1, 2, 3, 5):** Must be located in the center. There is always a road surrounding it. The Main Pipe Rack connects to it.\n    \n- **Cooling Tower (Unit 12):** An important rule — it must be at least 50m away from the Admin Building.\n    \n- **Admin Building (Unit 28):** Must be positioned 20m away from the power units and with its back facing the wind direction.\n    \n\n**3. Utility Connections (Pipe Racks):**\n\n- The **Main Rack** has a fixed width of 8m, while the others are 6m.\n    \n- These are the lines that connect your blocks.","x":2880,"y":410,"width":884,"height":536},
		{"id":"2bb0e95c7eb7a3c9","type":"text","text":"Overview_Canvas - \nvisual map of the whole project","x":-600,"y":1461,"width":250,"height":103},
		{"id":"4db1925fc20d2c19","type":"text","text":"Layout_Gen_Design/              ← your Obsidian vault (already exists)\n│\n├── Canvas/\n│   └── overview.canvas         ← visual map of the whole project (drag & drop)\n│\n├── !Product_Vision.md           ← what is this project? what is the final goal?\n├── !Scoring_Logic.md            ← how do we score a layout? what makes it good?\n│\n├── Prototype/\n│   └── scratch.md               ← rough ideas, first sketches, nothing is final\n│\n├── Step_01/\n│   ├── Plan.md                  ← what exactly does Step 01 do? inputs, outputs\n│   ├── Group_PowerBlock.md      ← rules: \"place at center, surround with road...\"\n│   ├── Group_CoolingTower.md    ← rules: \"place on wind direction side...\"\n│   └── Group_GIS.md             ← rules: \"near Power Block transformers...\"\n│\n└── Step_02/\n    └── Plan.md                  ← empty for now — fill in later","x":-600,"y":721,"width":841,"height":700},
		{"id":"5b0f19c9511d7b9f","type":"file","file":"01_Products/Layout_Gen_Design/Pipeline/Phase_01/Main Ideas.md","x":520,"y":285,"width":745,"height":595}
